<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Sept 24.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Sept 24.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF SEPTEMBER 24 VERSUS SEPTEMBER 17, 1996	 DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   36/11    2/1     178/233  133/105  349/350    217</p>
<p> SASK.	3/3     0/0	60/61    14/8     77/72	46</p>
<p> B.C.	 4/2     0/1	13/18    18/14    35/35	11</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	2/2	4/4	  0</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 1/2	0/0	1/2	  1</p>
<p> TOTAL     43/16    2/2     254/316  167/129  466/463    275</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>-- Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624</p>
